Course: CS2102 - IITPSx Processor Project

CLAIMS DECLARATION:

1. Assembler (asm.c):
   - Written in strict ISO C89 (compiles with -std=c89 -pedantic -W -Wall).
   - Implements two-pass assembly for symbol resolution and displacement.
   - Detects duplicate labels, missing labels, and unknown instructions.
   - Generates binary object files (.o) starting at address zero.
   - Produces formatted listing files (.lst).
   - Implemented arithmetic extension instructions: mul and div.

2. Emulator (emu.c):
   - Loads binary object files into simulated memory.
   - Correctly simulates registers A, B, PC, SP, and memory.
   - Implements full instruction set execution including mul and div.
   - Detects runtime errors (e.g., division by zero).

3. Assembly Programs & Tests:
   - Completed functional bubble.asm program.
   - Created test cases for arithmetic, arithmetic extension (mul/div), and error diagnostic test cases.